      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial BCC solid solution is metastable and has a high dislocation density.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ball-milled powder may contain oxygen contamination.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7866258::rubric_effects::000::f41c1717b0"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An SPS temperature window of 850–950 °C optimizes secondary-phase precipitation in Mg-Al-Ti-V-Fe-Co.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SPS in this window produces a continuous nanoscale network of refractory-rich intermetallics.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::rubric_effects::002::065b5a3f8d",
        "PMC7866258::rubric_effects::000::f41c1717b0"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates are Ti-V-Fe-Co-rich Laves or B2-type phases located at grain boundaries and within the matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7866258::rubric_effects::000::f41c1717b0"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 850–950 °C, diffusion of Ti, V, Fe, and Co becomes sufficient to nucleate and grow stable intermetallics.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7866258::rubric_effects::000::f41c1717b0",
        "PMC7866258::rubric_effects::001::1589586d86"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping the SPS temperature at or below 950 °C prevents significant Mg evaporation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intermetallic network slows both oxygen ingress and Mg outward diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::rubric_effects::002::065b5a3f8d",
        "PMC9955357::rubric_effects::005::0730566db4"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The diffusion barriers promote formation of a dense, protective oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::rubric_effects::002::065b5a3f8d",
        "PMC9955357::rubric_effects::005::0730566db4"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitated network prevents pore coalescence during SPS.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Material sintered in the proposed window will exceed 98% theoretical density.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Material sintered in the proposed window will have Vickers hardness above 600 HV.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::rubric_effects::002::065b5a3f8d"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy will exhibit oxidation weight gain below 5 mg/cm² after 50 h at 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::rubric_effects::002::065b5a3f8d"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation will produce a uniform Cr/Fe-rich passive film.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above 980 °C, rapid Mg volatilization causes composition deviation and failure of the proposed mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Below 820 °C, diffusion is too slow to form a continuous intermetallic network, resulting in porosity and poor barrier properties.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti, V, Fe, and Co have higher diffusion activation energies than Mg, enabling selective precipitation before Mg loss dominates.",
